---
import AutomaticPocketLayout from "../../layouts/AutomaticPocketLayout.astro";
---

<AutomaticPocketLayout
  title="Automatic Pocket"
  description="A drummer to practise bass with: 36 beats on a real kit, with fills, switch-ups and drop-outs. Pick a beat, press Play, and play."
>
  <p class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] italic text-2xl leading-snug text-[color:var(--color-ink-soft)]">
    A drummer to practise bass with. Pick a beat, press Play, and play.
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:gap-8 my-10">
    <figure class="!my-0">
      <img
        src="/images/automatic-pocket/drums.jpg"
        width="640" height="1391"
        alt="The drums playing: a Rock beat at 90 bpm, bar 12 of the A section, four beat lights, and the kick pattern with a line moving across it."
        class="rounded-[1.6rem] shadow-[0_10px_30px_rgba(44,24,16,0.25)]"
      />
      <figcaption>While it plays: the bar you're in, and the kick pattern with a line moving in time.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="!my-0">
      <img
        src="/images/automatic-pocket/drummer.jpg"
        width="640" height="1391"
        alt="The drummer settings: plays a fill every 8 bars, half a bar, rock fills; switches it up every 8 bars with the kick staying; never drops out; holds the tempo steady."
        class="rounded-[1.6rem] shadow-[0_10px_30px_rgba(44,24,16,0.25)]"
      />
      <figcaption>The drummer: fills, switch-ups, drop-outs and tempo drift.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    Pick a beat, set the tempo and press Play. The drums are recorded on a real kit, and the
    drummer behaves like one: a fill at the end of the phrase, a switch to the ride for the next
    section, a crash on the way back in. Change the beat, the tempo or what the drummer's doing
    while it plays, and it picks up on the same beat of the same bar. It works on the speaker or
    in headphones, with nothing to set up.
  </p>

  <h2>What's in it</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc">
    <li>36 beats: rock and pop, funk and soul, hip-hop and electronic, Latin and Caribbean, swing and shuffle, plus bare clicks for slow practice. Any tempo from 40 to 200.</li>
    <li>Fills written for each style, every 4, 8 or 16 bars, half a bar or a whole one.</li>
    <li>A B section every 8 or 16 bars, with the time moved to another cymbal and the kick kept or made busier.</li>
    <li>A drummer who can drop out for a few bars while you keep time on your own, or drift the tempo for you to follow.</li>
    <li>Your own beats: draw one on a step grid with ten drums, straight or triplet, with ghost notes and accents, or start from a copy of a built-in beat.</li>
    <li>Score my timing: put headphones on, play a note on every kick, and see how early or late each one was, which kicks you rush or drag, and a score for the take.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What you need</h2>
  <p>
    An iPhone or iPad. The drums play on the speaker or in headphones. To score your timing you also
    need headphones (wired, USB-C or Bluetooth) and your bass through an amp or played unplugged near
    the device. There's no account, and nothing leaves your device.
  </p>

  <p class="marginalia">
    <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/automatic-pocket/id6759693937">Free on the App Store</a>, for
    iPhone and iPad.
  </p>

  <p>
    Questions or problems: see <a href="/automatic-pocket/support">support</a>. How the app came to be
    is in its <a href="/specimens/automatic-pocket">specimen entry</a>.
  </p>
</AutomaticPocketLayout>
